# Agreements to the inbound terms stated in CONTRIBUTING.md. One line per
# contributor, in the order they arrived:
#
#     <github-login> <terms-version> <date-signed>
#
# Add your own line, in your own pull request, committed with
# `git commit -s`. That is the whole process: the line is the record and
# your commit is the signature. scripts/cla.sh reads this file and
# .github/workflows/cla.yml is what runs it on a pull request.
#
# Nobody with push access appears here. Being invited as a collaborator,
# or being a member of the organisation, is already an agreement -- and a
# maintainer cannot grant themselves a licence to their own copyright.
#
# The list is append-only. Editing or removing a line fails the check,
# because either would let one author drop somebody else's signature or
# backdate their own to terms they never read.
